      "title": "What Can I Do With This Major?",
      "description": "SUNY New Paltz | What Can I Do With This Major? Skip To Main Content Students Home Apply Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission International Admission Majors & Minors Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Parents Home Parent & Family Weekend Commencement Map & Directions Campus Safety Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Alumni Home Alumni Relations Give Today New Paltz Magazine Connect- Monthly E-Newsletter Directory Resources A-Z Index Brightspace Library Information Technology Services my.newpaltz.edu People Finder Microsoft 365 (Email) Academics Academic Calendar Schedule of Classes Undergraduate Catalog Majors & Minors Graduate Catalog Graduate Studies Professional Licensure Disclosures Advising Hub Library The Honors Program International Programs Admission Apply Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission International Admission What Can I Do With This Major? About Us Our Mission Accreditation Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Free Speech: Your Rights and Responsibilities Our Latest Rankings Visitor's Guide Employment Campus Life Hawks Athletics Wellness & Recreation The Dorsky Museum Theatre Box Office Residence Life On-Campus Dining Campus Bookstore New Paltz Engage Visit Apply Give What Can I Do With This Major? New Paltz » What Can I Do With This Major? What Can I Do With This Major? Explore potential careers for your New Paltz major. See what New Paltz Alumni are doing with their degrees. The School of Business The School of Business is an accredited member of the Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business (AACSB), a distinction reserved for just the top 5 percent of business schools worldwide. Careers In Accounting Careers in Finance Careers In International General Business Careers In Management Careers In Marketing The School of Education State-of-the-art classrooms, an expanded Curriculum Materials Center, and remodeled Literacy Center offers students a range of opportunities to collborate with faculty and connect theory with policy and practice. Careers In Education The School of Fine & Performing Arts Nationally accredited programs in art education, art history, art studio, music, and theatre arts are taught by dedicated faculty who bring decades of experience in creative work, performance, and independent scholarship in the classroom. Careers In Fine Arts Careers In Art History Careers In Graphic Design Careers In Theatre Careers In Music The College of Liberal Arts & Sciences Home to 17 departments and interdisciplinary programs, the College of Liberal Arts & Sciences offers eleven interdisciplinary minor curricula from all five schools, where students develop the timeless knowledge and skills of a liberal education. Careers In Anthropology Careers In Asian Studies Careers In Black Studies Careers In Communication Disorders Careers In Communication Studies Careers In English Careers In Economics Careers In French Careers In Geography Careers In History Careers In International Relations Careers In Journalism Careers In Digital Media Careers In Philosophy Careers In Political Science Careers In Psychology Careers In Sociology Careers In Spanish Careers In Women's, Gender and Sexuality Studies School of Science & Engineering The School provides a rigorous education in math, science and engineering with an emphasis on problem-solving, creative thinking and teamwork. Faculty/student undergraduate research and design projects are emphasized throughout the School. Careers In Biochemistry Careers In Biology Careers In Chemistry Careers In Computer Engineering Careers In Computer Science Careers In Environmental Science Careers In Electrical Engineering Careers in Geology Careers In Mathematics Careers In Mechanical Engineering Careers In Physics/Astronomy Employment as an International Student As a non-immigrant on an F –1 student visa, in the United States, you may have the option to engage in practical training during your program or after it ends. Practical training can provide valuable work experience by sharpening and adding to the skills you are learning at SUNY New Paltz. There are two types of practical training opportunities available for F-1 students: curricular practical training (CPT) and optional practical training (OPT). Both CPT, and OPT are a benefit of maintaining your F-1 status. While on CPT or OPT, students are still in F-1 student status, and the International Student Services Office continues to provide F-1 student status support while completing their practical training opportunity. Employment as an International Student SUNY New Paltz 1 Hawk Drive New Paltz, NY 12561 845-257-SUNY (7869) 877-MY-NP-411 (toll free) College of Liberal Arts & Sciences School of Business School of Education School of Fine & Performing Arts School of Science & Engineering Graduate, Professional & Interdisciplinary Studies International Programs A-Z Listing Academic Calendar Alumni Relations Apply Bias Reporting Form Construction Update Diversity, Equity and Inclusion Directory Events Emergency Cancellations and Delays Policy Emergency Response Plan Employment Financial Aid Foundation & Support Free Speech: Your Rights and Responsibilities Information Technology Services Maps, Directions & Parking Office Hours & Availability Privacy Policy Site Map Report an Accessibility Issue TerminalFour Login University Police Visit Us"
