      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Employment Opportunities | SUNY New Paltz Skip To Main Content Students Home Apply Undergraduate Admission Transfer Student Essentials Graduate Admission International Admission Majors & Minors Scholarships Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Virtual Tour Parents Home Parent & Family Weekend Commencement Map & Directions Campus Safety Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Alumni Home Alumni Relations Give Today New Paltz Magazine Connect- Monthly E-Newsletter Donors Ways to Give Planned Giving Foundation Contact Us Directory Resources A-Z Index Brightspace Library Information Technology Services my.newpaltz.edu People Finder Microsoft 365 (Email) Academics Academic Calendar Schedule of Classes Undergraduate Catalog Majors & Minors Graduate Catalog Graduate Studies Professional Licensure Disclosures Advising Hub Library The Honors Program International Programs Admission Apply Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission International Admission What Can I Do With This Major? About Us Our Mission Accreditation Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Free Speech: Your Rights and Responsibilities Our Latest Rankings Visitor's Guide Employment Campus Life Hawks Athletics Wellness & Recreation The Dorsky Museum Career Resource Center Box Office Residence Life On-Campus Dining Campus Bookstore Visit Apply Give New Paltz » Office of Human Resources, Diversity & Inclusion » Employment Opportunities Office of Human Resources, Diversity & Inclusion Resources Accommodations (ADA) Accommodations (ADA) Accessibility Guide for Events Benefits Collective Bargaining Agreements Diversity, Equity & Inclusion Diversity LGBTQ Community Sustainability Employment Opportunities Employment Opportunities Live & Work With Us More About SUNY New Paltz Meet The Leadership Institutional Profile Benefits Information for Prospective Hires Ethics Forms Holiday Calendar 2026 Holiday Calendar 2025 Holiday Calendar 2024 HR Staff Immigration Support for Employees Leave Policies & Procedures, Resources, and Information Public Officers Law Book SUNY HR Acronyms SUNY Policies of the Board of Trustees Training & Development Useful Information for New Hires Who Do I Contact For... NYS Public Officers Law Book Ethics Handbook for NYS Employees Employment Opportunities This page is your source for professional, faculty, classified, and Research Foundation job vacancies at the State University of New York at New Paltz. This site is updated as soon as positions become available or have been filled. Please review the individual job posting for job specifications, required qualifications, deadline dates, and how to apply. Good Luck with your job search! View all vacancies (except adjunct and internal) Internal Vacancies External Vacancies Faculty Vacancies Part-time Adjunct Lecturer Vacancies Professional Vacancies Classified Service Vacancies Civil Service Examination Web Site SUNY New Paltz postings are also located on the board outside of the Credit Union in the Basement of the Haggerty Administration Building. Career Resource Center (job postings for students) Resources for Prospective Employees Questions regarding the search process, procedure, or various search forms may be directed to the Office of Compliance and Campus Climate at 845-257-3675. Applicant questions regarding faculty and non-civil-service staff openings or applications can be directed to Roderick Coffey, Recruiting & Onboarding Coordinator at [email protected] . Definitions: Internal Vacancy: Posted exclusively for members of the New Paltz campus. This practice is designed to allow eligible campus employees an opportunity for promotion before external candidates are considered. Employees currently employed in professional (UUP or Research Foundation) or classified (CSEA, PEF, Council 82) titles are eligible to apply for these positions. Internal vacancies can be viewed by faculty/staff who log in to my.newpaltz.edu . External Vacancy: Open to the public. Professional Vacancy: Administrative, non-teaching position. Classified Vacancy: Civil Service position. SUNY New Paltz 1 Hawk Drive New Paltz, NY 12561 845-257-SUNY (7869) 877-MY-NP-411 (toll free) College of Liberal Arts & Sciences School of Business School of Education School of Fine & Performing Arts School of Science & Engineering Graduate, Professional & Interdisciplinary Studies International Programs A-Z Listing Academic Calendar Alumni Relations Apply Bias Reporting Form Construction Update Diversity, Equity and Inclusion Directory Events Emergency Cancellations and Delays Policy Emergency Response Plan Employment Financial Aid Foundation & Support Free Speech: Your Rights and Responsibilities Information Technology Services Maps, Directions & Parking Office Hours & Availability Privacy Policy Site Map Report an Accessibility Issue TerminalFour Login University Police Visit Us"
    },
