      "description": "Benefits Information for Prospective Hires | SUNY New Paltz Skip To Main Content Students Home Apply Undergraduate Admission Transfer Student Essentials Graduate Admission International Admission Majors & Minors Scholarships Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Virtual Tour Parents Home Parent & Family Weekend Commencement Map & Directions Campus Safety Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Alumni Home Alumni Relations Give Today New Paltz Magazine Connect- Monthly E-Newsletter Donors Ways to Give Planned Giving Foundation Contact Us Directory Resources A-Z Index Brightspace Library Information Technology Services my.newpaltz.edu People Finder Microsoft 365 (Email) ☰ Academics Academic Calendar Schedule of Classes Undergraduate Catalog Majors & Minors Graduate Catalog Graduate Studies Professional Licensure Disclosures Advising Hub Library The Honors Program International Programs Admission Apply Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission International Admission What Can I Do With This Major? About Us Our Mission Accreditation Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Free Speech: Your Rights and Responsibilities Our Latest Rankings Visitor's Guide Employment Campus Life Hawks Athletics Wellness & Recreation The Dorsky Museum Career Resource Center Box Office Residence Life On-Campus Dining Campus Bookstore Visit Apply Give New Paltz » Office of Human Resources, Diversity & Inclusion » Employment Opportunities » Benefits Information for Prospective Hires Office of Human Resources, Diversity & Inclusion Resources Accommodations (ADA) Accommodations (ADA) Accessibility Guide for Events Benefits Collective Bargaining Agreements Diversity, Equity & Inclusion Diversity LGBTQ Community Sustainability Employment Opportunities Employment Opportunities Live & Work With Us More About SUNY New Paltz Meet The Leadership Institutional Profile Benefits Information for Prospective Hires Ethics Forms Holiday Calendar 2026 Holiday Calendar 2025 Holiday Calendar 2024 HR Staff Immigration Support for Employees Leave Policies & Procedures, Resources, and Information Public Officers Law Book SUNY HR Acronyms SUNY Policies of the Board of Trustees Training & Development Useful Information for New Hires Who Do I Contact For... NYS Public Officers Law Book Ethics Handbook for NYS Employees Benefits Information for Prospective Hires Under the SUNY system , SUNY New Paltz offers full New York State benefits which are among the most comprehensive in the country. Employees must have a full-time appointment that is expected to last 3 months or longer, or a part-time appointment that is at least half-time (.5 FTE) and is expected to last 3 months or longer. While all benefits packages here are full and comprehensive, the packages are delineated according to the bargaining group the appointment comes under. There are very small differences not in the coverage of benefits, but in how certain parts of them are applied. Below you will find information regarding the specific benefits arrangements for each group. If you took a civil service examination to qualify for your interview, you will be under CSEA, otherwise known as Classified hires (Civil Service) . If you are applying for a faculty or staff role, more than likely you will be a part of UUP, and beholden to their full-time benefits schedule , or part-time  benefits schedule . Your role may be Management Confidential (M/C); ask the search chair you are communicating with if this is the case. Other perks of working at SUNY New Paltz will vary depending on your bargaining unit, but they can include and are not necessarily limited to: Free or discounted classes and trainings Multiple discount programs on everything from household items to resort vacations Comprehensive retirement (pension) program Very generous Vacation and Sick leave accrual And much, much more! SUNY New Paltz 1 Hawk Drive New Paltz, NY 12561 845-257-SUNY (7869) 877-MY-NP-411 (toll free) College of Liberal Arts & Sciences School of Business School of Education School of Fine & Performing Arts School of Science & Engineering Graduate, Professional & Interdisciplinary Studies International Programs A-Z Listing Academic Calendar Alumni Relations Apply Bias Reporting Form Construction Update Diversity, Equity and Inclusion Directory Events Emergency Cancellations and Delays Policy Emergency Response Plan Employment Financial Aid Foundation & Support Free Speech: Your Rights and Responsibilities Information Technology Services Maps, Directions & Parking Office Hours & Availability Privacy Policy Site Map Report an Accessibility Issue TerminalFour Login University Police Visit Us"
    }
